A JSON outline lists the keys of the root object without their quotes: scalar values print after the key as written, escapes included; objects and arrays print only the key, and the empty key keeps its quotes.
tree-sitter-json parses comments, as `tsconfig.json` files use them: a leading comment is the header, and one directly above a key starts its line range.
== args
input/tsconfig.json
== file input/tsconfig.json
// TypeScript settings for the demo.
{
  // Compiler settings.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "name": "line\nbreak",
  "": 0,
  "count": 3
}
== stdout
input/tsconfig.json
TypeScript settings for the demo.
[L3-L6] compilerOptions
[L7-L7] include
[L8-L8] name: "line\nbreak"
[L9-L9] "": 0
[L10-L10] count: 3
